1
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:11,400
So, Zekken shows up at 3 o 'clock
on this island on Floor 24. Mm-hmm.

2
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,977
Then I'll see you guys
there tomorrow at 2.30.

3
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:15,660
You got it! I can't wait!

4
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,377
This will be so much fun!

5
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:19,000
Yeah, it will! Ha, yeah!

6
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,357
The Berserk Healer's gonna get unleashed!

7
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:25,200
Daddy, you have something
on your face! Huh? For real?

8
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:27,857
Yes, it's covered in ink! You're kidding!

9
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,057
See you guys tomorrow!

10
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,620
Yeah, see ya!

11
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,780
I don't know.

12
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:33,640
I've never been in the sky,
but I haven't been in the sky,

13
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:38,580
but I haven't been able to reach my feet.

14
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:43,660
I've never seen the cold,
but I've never seen the rain.

15
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:47,637
I don't regret anything,

16
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,617
but the sound of the sound

17
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:55,760
is coming from the sky.

18
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:03,097
This story is the beginning of the song.

19
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:07,277
We are connected to
the end of the journey.

20
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:10,477
You can create the world of the future.

21
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:15,500
We are in the sky in the sky.

22
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,797
Two pieces of the dream.

23
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:23,080
One piece of the dream.

24
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,060
Oh?

25
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:03,734
Good night, Miss Sara.

26
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,257
Thank you for coming.

27
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,340
I'm sorry you had to work so late.

28
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,017
Not at all, really.

29
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,640
Just doing my job, miss.

30
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,857
Do you know if my mother
and brother are home yet?

31
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:21,697
Koichi wrote a phone to say he
won't be in until late tonight.

32
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:24,800
And your mother is waiting
in the dining room.

33
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,637
Oh, thank you.

34
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,426
Have a good night, Miss Sara.

35
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,540
You're late.

36
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,606
Next time, I want you
here five minutes early.

37
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:05,740
Yes, ma 'am.

38
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:24,460
It looks good.

39
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,240
I assume you were using that thing again?

40
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,990
Yes.

41
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:51,041
My friends and I were doing
our homework together.

42
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:55,777
Unless you actually physically do your
homework, you won't learn a thing.

43
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:58,137
But we all live so far
away from each other.

44
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,737
It's more convenient
for us to meet in-game.

45
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:04,114
It hardly qualifies as meeting
if you're using that toy.

46
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,917
Besides, doing your homework
is not a team activity.

47
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,118
If you're with your friends,
you'll just fool around.

48
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:15,500
Asuna, you don't have time
to play around anymore.

49
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,135
You're two years behind everyone else.

50
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:22,277
You should be studying as hard as you
can to make up for all that lost time.

51
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,840
But I am studying hard.

52
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:26,597
Didn't you see my grades
for the second semester?

53
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,151
I left them on your desk.

54
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:29,740
Yes, I saw them.

55
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:33,520
But grades from a school like
that are suspect at best.

56
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,180
They're not suspect?

57
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:38,170
Yes, Will.

58
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:41,657
For your next trimester, I've
decided to hire you a tutor.

59
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:44,757
And not one of those virtual
ones everyone's going on about.

60
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,357
Someone who'll come to the house.

61
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,820
But don't I get to have any say in it?

62
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,356
Have a look at this.

63
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:57,480
A transfer exam study guide?

64
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:00,965
I know someone on the
board of directors there.

65
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:02,197
After some discussion,

66
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:06,397
I convinced them to let you take an exam
to transfer into their senior class.

67
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:10,240
It's a proper high school,
not some makeshift study hall.

68
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,117
And since it's credit-based,

69
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:15,717
I'm sure you'll be able to
graduate after the first trimester.

70
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,557
If you do, you'll be back
on track for college.

71
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,477
Wait, hold on!

72
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:22,397
You can't just make a
decision like this without me.

73
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,540
I happen to like the school I'm in.

74
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,486
The teachers there are great.

75
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,797
I can learn there just
as much as anywhere.

76
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,704
I don't have to change schools.

77
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,702
I've done my research, you know.

78
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:40,897
And believe me, that place you're
attending can hardly be called a school.

79
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:44,320
The curriculum is slapdash
and the classes are a joke.

80
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:46,497
Even the faculty is substandard.

81
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:50,286
They're a bunch of losers with
no real credentials to speak of.

82
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,460
Don't say that.

83
00:06:56,320 --> 00:07:00,377
They claim they're helping the students
who fell behind because of that accident.

84
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:01,480
It's all a lie.

85
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:04,077
They just want all the
children who've spent the last

86
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:07,278
two years killing each other
in one convenient place.

87
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,020
So they can monitor them.

88
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,514
It's more like an asylum than a school.

89
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,960
Did you forget, Mother?

90
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:18,051
I spent two years killing other kids, too.

91
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,337
All the friends you
had back in junior high

92
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,677
are studying to get
into college this year.

93
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,348
They're leaving you behind.

94
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,852
Doesn't that bother you?

95
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:30,240
Not at all.

96
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:34,537
If it takes an extra year or two,
it won't make much of a difference.

97
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:37,149
Besides, I might not
want to go to college.

98
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,550
Ridiculous.

99
00:07:38,633 --> 00:07:40,127
I won't entertain such talk.

100
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,854
You're far too gifted.

101
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,137
And your father and I have gone to
great lengths to nurture your talents.

102
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:46,860
I hope you appreciate that.

103
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:50,297
I do, but shouldn't I get to
have a say in my own future?

104
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,897
Sure, I might not know what
kind of career I want right now,

105
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,557
but I'm close to finding out.

106
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:59,111
If I stay in my school for another year,
it will help me make that decision.

107
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:05,377
No matter how long you stay at a place
like that, it'll just limit your options.

108
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,737
Look, try to understand.

109
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,917
I don't want you to make a wrong
turn now and regret it later.

110
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,377
I just want you to have
a good life and find

111
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,989
yourself a good career
you can be proud of.

112
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:18,317
So that boy you forced me
to meet on New Year's Day,

113
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:21,097
that was you trying to
help me with my career?

114
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,497
You should have heard him.

115
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,657
He was talking like we were
already engaged or something.

116
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:29,681
You're the one who's limiting my
options, not me and not my school.

117
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,882
Marriage is part of your career.

118
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:40,880
If you marry beneath you, or marry
poor, I guarantee you'll regret it.

119
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:45,495
You won't have the means to pursue
whatever it is you really want to do.

120
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:48,637
That's why I think Yu-Yu
would be an excellent choice.

121
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:51,080
His family owns a small regional bank.

122
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:55,652
Those are much more stable than some
mega-bank run by a board of directors.

123
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,540
Your last choice wasn't very good.

124
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:06,036
Did you forget how he made me, and
I don't know how many others suffer?

125
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,740
Nobuyuki Tsuko nearly bankrupted Ragout.

126
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,780
He was your choice, mother.

127
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,578
Enough, young lady!

128
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:15,780
I don't want to hear about
him in this house again.

129
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:16,900
And you're wrong.

130
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,197
It wasn't my choice, it was your father's.

131
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:21,897
He suggested that crook
marry into this family.

132
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:24,157
He's never been a good judge of character.

133
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,280
But don't worry.

134
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,997
Yuya might lack initiative,
but he seems stable.

135
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,727
And stability is the
cornerstone of marriage.

136
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,060
I don't care.

137
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,337
I have no intention to date or marry him.

138
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:36,140
I choose who I'll marry.

139
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:41,387
Fine, as long as the man you choose is
from a good family and is worthy of you.

140
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:46,620
However, a boy like that, your little
friend from school, is not worthy.

141
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,580
You had him investigated?

142
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,100
Of course I did.

143
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:58,497
Try to understand, your father and I
only want what's best for you in life.

144
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:01,137
You have the potential
to do whatever you want,

145
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:03,455
as long as you make the right choices.

146
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,953
I need time to think about transferring.

147
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:13,674
Keep in mind, the deadline's next week.

148
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:16,746
Don't forget, and after
you fill out the form,

149
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:20,333
make three copies and leave
them in my office on my desk.

150
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:22,750
Mother.

151
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,500
What is it?

152
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:30,297
Even though they're gone, you're still
ashamed of Grandma and Grandpa, aren't you?

153
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:33,909
You're angry you weren't born
into a rich, important family.

154
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:36,830
Asuna!

155
00:10:36,913 --> 00:10:38,131
Come back here right now!

156
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,490
Asuna!

157
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,390
Kirito!

158
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,660
Hey, about that questionnaire.

159
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,017
Have you figured out
what you want to do yet?

160
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:08,100
I guess, if anything, I want to go from
playing games to being a creator. A creator?

161
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:09,640
What, for games?

162
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,200
No, not for games.

163
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:15,497
I want to make a human-machine interface
to replace the full-dive tech we use now.

164
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:18,377
I've been going to all these tech
forums to learn more about it,

165
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:21,401
but it's a heck of a lot
of information to absorb.

166
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:27,220
I want to be with Kirito
and go after the same dream.

167
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,210
But now...

168
00:11:29,293 --> 00:11:33,280
You sure are strong,
way stronger than I am.

169
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,300
I'm not strong at all.

170
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:39,640
In that world, I was a warrior.

171
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:46,980
But here, Lightning Flash Asuna of
the Knights of the Blood Oath is gone.

172
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:53,480
In the real world, I
don't have any real power.

173
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:12,637
It's rare for you to be so
punctual, don't you think?

174
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,960
It happens sometimes.

175
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,739
Hey, you remember?

176
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:47,237
You know, that one day you came to my
place in Selmburg and I made you dinner?

177
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:50,677
Hate to say it, but my memory's
about as good as my punctuality.

178
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:51,590
What?

179
00:12:52,420 --> 00:12:55,244
Yeah, I remember that day
like it was yesterday.

180
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:57,260
Really? Of course.

181
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,817
Let's see that's the day
I got a super rare food

182
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,782
item right and you made
an awesome stew out of it

183
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,840
That was some tasty meat.

184
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:09,140
I'm never gonna forget that day

185
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:13,416
You don't remember anything
except that stupid dinner?

186
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:22,080
It's almost time I better get over there!

187
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:25,760
Asuna be careful with second.

188
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:32,820
Well, it's like, Zekin's really
strong. Just saying. Don't you worry.

189
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:35,786
Listen, the others already
told me everything.

190
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,451
Yep, they even told me about how you lost.

191
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,031
I still can't believe it.

192
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,760
Oh, by the way,

193
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:45,437
Leafa said in the middle of your duel
with Zekken you stopped fighting to talk.

194
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:46,814
What'd you talk about?

195
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:51,000
Well, actually I asked
a question. What about?

196
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:56,020
I got a weird vibe, so I asked.

197
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:59,357
You're full-time in this
world, aren't you, Zekken?

198
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:03,960
And then, for an answer, I got a
sly grin and a mega-fast attack.

199
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:07,880
I'd never seen anything move that fast.

200
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:11,187
What did you mean by
full-time in this world?

201
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:13,967
Is that the same thing
as being a heavy user?

202
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:15,810
Uh-uh.

203
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:19,697
Zekin's way different than your
average everyday hardcore gamer.

204
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:20,957
It felt like...

205
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:25,097
like they were a sort of product of
the full-dive environment itself.

206
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,592
I have no idea what you're talking about.

207
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:30,372
In a way, it's probably better you don't.

208
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:34,555
The best way to explain it
is for you to experience it.

209
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,967
Every time we turn around, you're
always pawing at each other.

210
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,397
Sorry to interrupt your little love fest,

211
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,597
but there's a duel that's
supposed to be happening.

212
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:50,510
Yeah!

213
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,700
I know, I was on my way.

214
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,940
I yield! I quit! Resign!

215
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,420
Hi-ya!

216
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,340
That's 67 wins in a row!

217
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,180
Second undefeated!

218
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:50,480
Excuse me, Liz. What?

219
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:53,117
You asked me seconds a girl!

220
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,057
I didn't!

221
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:55,637
I could have sworn! I did!

222
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,577
You didn't!

223
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,817
And you!

224
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:01,997
I have a feeling! I
know! Why you lost? Now!

225
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:04,777
No!

226
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:07,297
You're wrong!

227
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:08,817
I didn't go easy on her!

228
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:09,730
Because she's a girl!

229
00:16:09,813 --> 00:16:11,137
I was going full out!

230
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,050
I swear!

231
00:16:12,133 --> 00:16:14,397
Halfway through our duel! Anyway!

232
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,200
Whatever!

233
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:23,200
So, uh, is there anyone else out there
want to take me on today? You're up.

234
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:24,262
Go on, get her.

235
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,757
Wait, I gotta psych myself up first.

236
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:30,437
Oh, please, once you cross swords with
her, believe me, you'll get psyched up.

237
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,140
Go on, get in there!

238
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,740
Hey, what's up? You next?

239
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:42,117
Oh, uh, hi.

240
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,600
I guess I am.

241
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:45,170
Awesome!

242
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:58,200
So, uh, does anything go
in this duel? Of course!

243
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:01,320
You can use magic or
items, whatever you want.

244
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:04,258
I'm only gonna use my sword, though.

245
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,280
Oh, wait. Almost forgot.

246
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:11,697
You want to fight on the
ground or in the air?

247
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:14,080
Is ether okay? Mm-hmm.

248
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:20,240
Let's duel on the ground then
you got it jumping's allowed,

249
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:22,260
but no using your wings, okay?

250
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,880
I don't know.

251
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:22,200
She is strong, but if I gave up now,
I'd ruin my reputation as a Swordsman.

252
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,660
In that world, I was a warrior.

253
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,080
But here?

254
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,030
Ah!

255
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,570
Mm…

256
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,030
Uh-oh!

257
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,270
Got her!

258
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,520
She saw my quadruple pain?

259
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,540
No way!

260
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,300
I won't lose!

261
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,500
Is this the Head combo?

262
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:27,260
Her original sword skill!

263
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:32,553
If I'm going to lose, it might as well
be to something as awesome as that!

264
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,060
That was an awesome fight, girl!

265
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,849
You're definitely the one!

266
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:03,930
Uh, what?

267
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,882
Aren't we gonna finish the duel?

268
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:10,277
I totally seen enough to
know you got what it takes.

269
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:12,419
But if you want, we can keep going.

270
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:19,397
I've been looking for someone
who could go the distance.

271
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,000
At last, I found you.

272
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:39,430
Mommy?

273
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:43,280
Asuna, where are you going? Asuna!

274
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:57,420
I picked ya, cause you're
the only one who can help us!

275
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,400
Help? With what?

276
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:18,060
Thank you.

277
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:51,037
I don't want to go.

278
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:54,280
I tend to be lazy to call.

279
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:00,577
You are sure?

280
00:23:00,660 --> 00:23:01,490
I'm never wrong.

281
00:23:01,573 --> 00:23:03,277
I have to be close to you.

282
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:04,397
I didn't see light.

283
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:10,900
I'm not okay.

284
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:16,097
I'm never wrong. I'm never wrong.

285
00:23:16,180 --> 00:23:19,160
I want to see how many times I can hear?

286
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:25,120
I want to see how many times I can hear?

287
00:23:36,180 --> 00:23:38,440
Next time, the Sleeping Knights.
